hb
==
    _______ 
   |x--|   |
   |o--|1--|
   |   |2--|
   |___|__/ 

hb can be used to hold txt databases such as ledger and todo.txt.

hb provides syncing capabilities to your notebook. Either via VCS or rsync.

Additional sync capabilities can be provided by 

You may like hb if you do any of the following,

* Manage personal finance with ledger
* Write todo's in todo.txt
* Write blogs

Usage
-----

hb is a framework that makes storing and retrieving text related information
effortless. Start by,

     $ hb new relative-folder/note.txt

This creates a note.txt under relative-folder/. Sometimes you may want to
import a note from your filesystem under hb, To do that use,
    
    $ hb new -m Downloads/recipe.txt
    $ hb new -c WorkingDir/somefile.txt

-m does a move operations, and -c does a copy operation.

After populating files inside hb, you can access them with,

    $ hb

Will start a fuzzy matcher if $FUZZER is set.  If $FUZZER is empty or not
found in $PATH. hb simply does `cd` to "$HB_PATH"

$HB_PATH should be pointed to the directory, where all the notes will end up.
If $HB_PATH is not provided, the ".local/share/notes" is used as $HB_PATH.

    $ hb sync

Does a commit, pull, push cycle in the notes folder.
